      "distinguishing_evidence": "notes/26 \u00a75c claims the framework cannot keep a dependent chain in registers, has no loop, and that UNROLL is capped at 32 (notes/06 C-16). A scan is the clean test because the chain IS the operator. The falsifier for class (i)/(iii) is the framework's own `cumsum` op: it exists, so 'the framework cannot express a scan' is false by inspection, and the live question becomes whether its lowering emits N dependent kernels or one. That is countable on the device, and notes/06 C-22 is the correction that says a CENSUS is not a measurement -- so the count is reported as context and the TIME is the evidence.",
